    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d270">

                <pb facs="0405" n="293" sameAs="frus:frus1910/pg293"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 774/693.</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Ambassador Rockhill to the Secretary of
                    State.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >American Embassy</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">St.
                                Petersburg</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1910-01-29"><hi rendition="#italic">January 29,
                        1910</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Referring to the department’s circular
                    instruction entitled “International Opium Conference” (Sept. 1, 1909), and to
                    this Embassy’s No. 553 of September 22 reporting the communication of the
                    invitation to the Russian Government, I have now the honor to nclose in
                    duplicate copies and translations of a note received to-day, in which the
                    Russian ministry for foreign affairs approves in principle the aide-mémoire
                    proposing the conference, but with a reservation as to the article relating to
                    restrictions upon the cultivation of the poppy.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">W. W. Rockhill.</hi></signed></closer>



                <xi:include href="d270-a1.xml" xpointer="d270-a1"/>
